---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import researchPlaceholder from '../../assets/pathways/investigate.jpg';
import {groups,resources} from '../../data/researchResources';
import {disciplines} from '../../data/disciplines';
import DisciplineArt from '../../components/DisciplineArt.astro';
import {guideFor,workflows} from '../../data/researchGuides';
---
<Base title="Research Resources | MycoGeeky">
<section class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">INVESTIGATE / RESEARCH RESOURCES</p><h1>Follow the evidence. Find the tools.</h1><p class="lead">A field guide to the research ecosystem behind fungal names, specimens, sequences and scientific discoveries. You don't need a degree to start exploring it.</p><p class="resource-count">{resources.length} resources across {groups.length} research areas · <a href="#directory">Browse the directory ↓</a></p></section>
<section class="section soft"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">WHO DOES WHAT?</p><h2>Six ways to ask a better question.</h2><p class="resource-intro">These aren't rigid job titles. Many researchers do several kinds of work—and the same mushroom may need all of them.</p><div class="resource-roles discipline-card-grid">{disciplines.map(d=><a class="resource-role discipline-card" href={`/investigate/disciplines/${d.slug}/`}><DisciplineArt kind={d.icon} accent={d.accent}/><div class="discipline-card-copy"><p class="discipline-metaphor">{d.metaphor}</p><h3>{d.title}</h3><p class="resource-question">{d.question}</p><p>{d.summary}</p><span class="discipline-card-link">Learn more <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></div></a>)}</div><p class="resource-footnote">A phylogenetic tree may support a lineage, but it doesn't automatically create a species name. Taxonomic judgments and nomenclatural rules answer different questions.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" id="directory"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">THE RESEARCH DIRECTORY</p><h2>What are you trying to find out?</h2><p class="resource-intro">Start with a research task, or browse by subject. Every resource has a practical use, a stage in the research process, and a limitation worth knowing. Featured tools are prominent because of broad utility—not scientific rank.</p>
<div class="research-workflows"><div><p class="eyebrow">START WITH YOUR QUESTION</p><h3>Choose a research path</h3><div class="research-workflow-options">{workflows.map((w,i)=><button class="research-workflow-choice" type="button" data-workflow-button={w.id} aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'}>{w.label}</button>)}</div></div><div class="research-workflow-detail">{workflows.map((w,i)=><div data-workflow-panel={w.id} hidden={i!==0}><h3>{w.heading}</h3><ol>{w.steps.map(step=><li>{step}</li>)}</ol><p><strong>Open these first:</strong> {w.tools.map((name,i)=><span>{i>0?' · ':''}<a href={`#tool-${name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/-$/,'')}`}>{name}</a></span>)}</p></div>)}</div></div>
<nav class="resource-nav" aria-label="Research resource categories"><a href="#names">Names</a><a href="#specimens">Specimens</a><a href="#sequence">DNA & trees</a><a href="#field">Ecology</a><a href="#literature">Literature</a></nav>
{groups.map(group=><section class="resource-group" id={group.id}><div class="resource-group-head"><h3>{group.title}</h3><p>{group.intro}</p></div><div class="resource-cards research-tool-grid">{[...group.resources].sort((a,b)=>({featured:0,specialist:1,additional:2}[guideFor(a[0])?.tier||'additional']-({featured:0,specialist:1,additional:2}[guideFor(b[0])?.tier||'additional']))).map(([name,url,purpose,note,source])=>{const guide=guideFor(name);return <article id={`tool-${name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/-$/,'')}`} class={`resource-entry research-tool ${guide?.tier||'additional'}`}><div class="resource-entry-top"><h4><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h4>{guide?.tier==='featured'&&<span class="resource-origin">Common starting point</span>}</div>{guide?<><p class="research-tool-when"><strong>Use when:</strong> {guide.when}</p><ul>{guide.do.map(task=><li>{task}</li>)}</ul><p class="research-stage"><strong>Stage:</strong> {guide.stage.join(' → ')}</p></>:<p>{purpose}</p>}<p class="resource-caution"><strong>Keep in mind:</strong> {note}</p></article>})}</div></section>)}</div></section>
<script>
const buttons=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-workflow-button]');
const panels=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-workflow-panel]');
buttons.forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{const id=button.dataset.workflowButton;buttons.forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));panels.forEach(p=>{p.hidden=p.dataset.workflowPanel!==id})}));
</script>
<section class="section soft story-with-photo"><div class="container narrative-split"><div class="narrative-copy"><p class="eyebrow">START WITH THE SOURCE</p><h2>A practical guide to describing new fungal species.</h2><p class="resource-intro">This directory began with Aime and colleagues' 2021 guide, <em>How to publish a new fungal species, or name, version 3.0</em>. The paper distinguishes the formal requirements of nomenclature from taxonomic best practices, and its page 10 checklist follows the path from specimen and evidence to publication and repository updates.</p><p>Some resources above are named in that paper; others are additions for broader research workflows. The paper is from 2021, so always consult current software documentation, database policies and the current nomenclatural Code.</p><a class="button primary" href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s43008-021-00063-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the open-access paper ↗</a></div><figure class="narrative-photo"><Image src={researchPlaceholder} alt="Documenting mushrooms in the field — temporary editorial image" widths={[480,800]} sizes="(max-width:800px) 100vw, 40vw"/><figcaption>IMAGE PLACEHOLDER · Replace with specimen notes, a herbarium voucher, or your own microscopy photograph</figcaption></figure></div></section>
</Base>
